# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you need:  cp .env.example .env
#
# EVERY value here is optional. With an empty .env the app runs end to end:
# subscriptions grant a local dev unlock, analytics and attribution no-op, ads
# stay off. Add a key to switch that service on. No code changes needed.
#
# ⚠️  EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are INLINED INTO THE APP BUNDLE at build time and
#    are readable by anyone who downloads your app. Every key below is a
#    *publishable* client key, which is why they can live here. Never put a
#    RevenueCat secret key, a PostHog personal API key, or any server
#    credential in this file. See constants/config.ts.
#
# ⚠️  Metro caches env values. After editing .env, restart with `npx expo start -c`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=My App

# Numeric Apple App ID: the digits in your App Store URL (…/id6760719879).
# Needed by AppsFlyer for SKAdNetwork and by the "write a review" link.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_APPLE_APP_ID=

# ── RevenueCat, subscriptions ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard → Project → API keys → *public* SDK keys (appl_… / goog_…).
# Leave both blank while building: purchase() grants a local dev unlock instead,
# so the paywall and every gated feature stay testable. See docs/revenuecat.md.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=appl_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=goog_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Entitlement identifier, exactly as spelled in RevenueCat → Entitlements.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_RC_ENTITLEMENT=pro

# Offering to show on the paywall. Blank = whichever offering RC marks "current",
# which is what you want: it lets you swap pricing without an app release.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_RC_OFFERING=

# ── AppsFlyer, ad attribution ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One dev key per AppsFlyer account, shared by all your apps.
# AppsFlyer → Settings → App settings → Dev key.
# Only worth setting if you run paid ads. See docs/appsflyer.md, and read
# docs/launch-checklist.md before your first campaign: the dashboard-side setup
# is where attribution actually goes wrong, not the code.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_APPSFLYER_DEV_KEY=

# ── PostHog, product analytics ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project settings → Project API key (starts `phc_`). Safe to ship publicly.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# EU cloud users: https://eu.i.posthog.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# ── AdMob, ads ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ads stay off unless this is exactly "true". Google's test unit IDs are wired
# in, so you can turn ads on with no AdMob account. Serving REAL ads to yourself
# is how accounts get banned, keep the test IDs until you ship.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ADS_ENABLED=false
# The `~` App IDs from AdMob → Apps → App settings (not the `/` ad-unit IDs):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMOB_IOS_APP_ID=ca-app-pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx~xxxxxxxxxx
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMOB_ANDROID_APP_ID=ca-app-pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx~xxxxxxxxxx

# ── App Tracking Transparency ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shows Apple's IDFA prompt on iOS. Only turn this on if you spend on ads.
# nothing here needs it, and it costs a beat of trust on first launch.
# Edit the explanation string in app.config.ts before submitting: App Review
# rejects generic wording. See lib/tracking.ts.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ATT_ENABLED=false
